cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "RINDTI: drug-target interaction prediction from protein residue interaction networks"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ilya
    family-names: Senatorov
    email: ilya.senatorov@helmholtz-hips.de
    affiliation: Helmholtz Institute for Pharmaceutical Research Saarland
repository-code: "https://github.com/ilsenatorov/rindti"
url: "https://rindti.readthedocs.io"
abstract: >-
  RINDTI predicts drug-target interactions by representing proteins as residue
  interaction networks (RINs) and drugs as molecular graphs, encoding both with
  graph neural networks. It ships a reproducible Snakemake pipeline that turns
  protein structures and interaction tables into ready-to-train graph datasets.
keywords:
  - drug-target interaction
  - graph neural networks
  - residue interaction network
  - structural bioinformatics
license: MIT
version: 2.0.0
